      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "buildJavaScript": "Follow these rules when generating code:\n- Create a single new function based on what the student planned in prompt.md. The function should update the vibe display and recovery display when an entry is logged.\n- The Recovery display should always end with \"hrs\" — that text is part of the function body, not a parameter.\n- Update the four button event listeners so each one calls the new function with the correct arguments for that entry.\n- Use only the parameters the student planned. Do not add extras.\n- Do not add loops, arrays, or conditional logic.\n- Keep the code structure and style consistent with what already exists in the file.\n- Do not modify any HTML or CSS.\n- Do not write additional helper functions."
      }
    },
    "bubble_choice_description": "Use AI to build a function that updates the app when a log entry is selected. Test different inputs and see how the output changes.",
    "long_instructions": "## Do This:\r\n\r\nThe Habit Lab app lets users log their daily vibe and how much recovery time they had. The buttons are wired up, but the function that updates the displays hasn't been written yet. Each entry has its own vibe and recovery hours, and the Recovery display should show the number followed by \"hrs.\"\r\n\r\nPlan in `spec.md`, then prompt the AI with your plan to generate the function. Test by clicking different entries.",
